13. Interactive Features: Popups & Labels


Popups appear when users click a marker:

leaflet() |&gt;
  addProviderTiles(providers$CartoDB.Positron) |&gt;
  addMarkers(
    lng = -105.08,
    lat = 40.57,
    popup = "CSU Campus",
    label = "Click me!"  # appear on hover
  )

Markers support HTML — embed tables, images, links:

leaflet() |&gt;
  addCircleMarkers(
    popup = ~paste0(
      "&lt;b&gt;", site_name, "&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;",
      "Flow: ", round(discharge, 2), " m&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;/sup&gt;/s"
    )
  )


Click marker to see popup:

18. NextRAD: Real-Time Precipitation WMS
WMS Tiles are pre-rendered map images from a server. Here we use NOAA/NEXRAD weather radar (Iowa Mesonet Program):

conus = filter(us_states(), !stusps %in% c("AK", "PR", "HI"))

leaflet() |&gt; 
  addProviderTiles(providers$CartoDB) |&gt; 
  addPolygons(data = st_union(conus), fillColor = "transparent",
              color = "black", weight = 1) |&gt; 
  addWMSTiles(
    "http://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/cgi-bin/wms/nexrad/n0r.cgi",
    layers = "nexrad-n0r-900913",
    options = WMSTileOptions(format = "image/png", transparent = TRUE)
  )

Why WMS? Real-time data (precipitation, radar), pre-rendered, responsive on mobile, server handles rendering.

20. leafem: Extended Leaflet + leafpop


Add interactive popups:

library(leaflet); library(leafpop)
library(sf)

quakes_sf &lt;- quakes |&gt;
  st_as_sf(
    coords = c("long", "lat"), 
    crs = 4326
  )

leaflet(quakes_sf) |&gt;
  addProviderTiles(
    providers$CartoDB
  ) |&gt;
  addCircleMarkers(
    radius = ~pmin(6, mag),
    color = "navy",
    popup = leafpop::popupTable(
      as.data.frame(quakes_sf),
      zcol = c("mag", "depth", 
               "stations")
    ),
    clusterOptions = 
      markerClusterOptions()
  ) |&gt;
  setView(180, -20, 3)






