A diagnostic trick: drop lon / lat and refit
If a feature is truly informative, dropping it should hurt the model.
If a feature is a spatial proxy, dropping it should only hurt under random CV — because under spatial CV the model couldn’t lean on it anyway.

recipe_no_xy &lt;- recipe(forested ~ ., data = forested_train) |&gt;
  step_rm(lon, lat) |&gt;
  step_impute_mean(all_numeric_predictors()) |&gt;
  step_dummy(all_nominal_predictors()) |&gt;
  step_normalize(all_numeric_predictors())

wf_no_xy &lt;- workflow() |&gt;
  add_recipe(recipe_no_xy) |&gt;
  add_model(log_mod)

set.seed(9)
rs_random_no_xy  &lt;- wf_no_xy |&gt;
  fit_resamples(resamples = forested_folds, metrics = metric_set(roc_auc))
rs_spatial_no_xy &lt;- wf_no_xy |&gt;
